# ==============================================================================
# .env FILE  (CertStudy)
# ==============================================================================
# How it works in Vite:
#   - Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to browser code
#     (via import.meta.env.NAME). Variables WITHOUT that prefix are NOT read by
#     the app in a local build; they exist here only for compatibility with the
#     Google AI Studio environment.
#   - To run 100% offline (localStorage), you do NOT need to fill in anything.
#     The app works without credentials; Google Drive/Docs is simply disabled.
#   - After changing this file, STOP and restart the dev server (npm run dev),
#     because Vite only reads .env at startup.
#   - NEVER commit this file with real values. It must stay in .gitignore.
#     Client Secrets must never be placed here (the app is a browser SPA and uses
#     only a public Client ID, with no secret).
# ==============================================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID  (the ONLY variable actually used in local development)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IT IS: the OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type "Web application") from Google Cloud.
#             Enables Google sign-in and Google Drive & Docs sync.
#             It is optional: without it the app runs normally offline via
#             localStorage.
#
# WHERE IT IS READ IN CODE: src/services/googleWorkspaceService.ts
#             (import.meta.env.VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID)
#
# WHERE TO GET IT (step by step):
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create/select a project.
#   2. Enable the APIs: "Google Drive API" and "Google Docs API"
#      (APIs & Services > Library).
#   3. Configure the OAuth consent screen (type External) with the scopes:
#        https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file
#        https://www.googleapis.com/auth/documents
#   4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create credentials >
#      "OAuth client ID" > type "Web application".
#   5. Under "Authorized JavaScript origins", add the EXACT URLs, with no
#      trailing slash:
#        http://localhost:3000
#        https://yourdomain.com             (e.g. your production domain)
#        https://your-username.github.io    (if publishing to GitHub Pages)
#   6. Copy the generated value. It has the format:
#        your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
#   7. Paste that value between the quotes below.
#
# ALTERNATIVE WITHOUT .env: you can also enter the Client ID directly in the app
#   UI (Settings), which stores it in localStorage under the key
#   "certstudy_custom_google_client_id". The priority order in the app is:
#   Client ID from the UI (localStorage) > VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID from .env.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY  (NOT used in the local Vite build, missing the VITE_ prefix)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IT IS: the Google Gemini API key used by the AI features
#             (question tutor, batch importer, notes copilot).
#
# IMPORTANT: this name WITHOUT the VITE_ prefix is NOT exposed to the browser by
#             Vite, so filling it in here has no effect on the local "npm run dev".
#             It exists for the Google AI Studio environment, which injects the
#             value automatically at runtime from the user's "secrets"
#             (Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI).
#
# WHERE TO GET IT (if you integrate it manually in the future): create a key at
#             https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#             For real local use, the key would have to be read via a VITE_
#             prefixed variable (e.g. VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY) and referenced in code.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_URL  (NOT used in the local Vite build, missing the VITE_ prefix)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IT IS: the public URL where the app is hosted. Used for self-referential
#             links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
#
# IMPORTANT: since it has no VITE_ prefix, it is not read locally by Vite.
#             In Google AI Studio it is injected automatically with the service
#             URL (Cloud Run). In your local environment, the origin used is
#             simply http://localhost:3000 (defined in vite.config.ts).
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"
